// TSThread's deque<unsigned long> (LLE TSThread +0x04..+0x18; its COMDATs sit in the first unit using it):
//  - members: allocator, _Map (+4), _Mapsize (+8), _Myoff (+0xc), _Mysize (+0x10); the ctor zeroes the four
//    inline (TSThread ctors 0x54203/0x5425d)
//  - blocks of _DEQUESIZ = 4096 / sizeof(T) elements (0x400 for 4-byte T); the map grows by max(_Mapsize / 2, 8)
//    slots (_Growmap 0x432d4, max_size() / _DEQUESIZ = 0xfffff). _Growmap never frees the old map: 0x432d4 calls
//    operator new and _Xlen only (with an operator delete(_Map) the register allocation differs, 76 -> exact)
//  - operator[](N) is begin()[N] (NEMessageManager::AbortXfer 0x413bd)
//  - iterators are {offset, container*}; operator* maps the offset through the map, wrapping at _Mapsize
//    (0x43f40)
//  - push_back 0x3dfdb, pop_front 0x438b0, pop_back 0x5b69c, _Tidy 0x43d85, ~deque 0x42f50 (pop_back until
//    empty, then _Tidy)
//  - range members (TSThread copy ctor / operator=, NELagLossSimulator.cpp): copy ctor 0x3de2a = insert(begin(),
//    X.begin(), X.end()); operator= 0x3de66 (copy + erase, or copy + insert(end(), ...)); erase(F, L) 0x3df0a
//    (shift the shorter side, then pop; returns `_M == 0 ? begin() : begin() + _M`); insert -> _Insert(P, F, L,
//    _Iter_cat(F)) 0x44119 (the later Dinkum four-case forward-iterator insert; the count comes from _Distance:
//    `_L - _F` inline gives a smaller frame); push_front 0x44392; iterator operator+ 0x4437d is `_Tmp += _N`;
//    const_iterator::operator== 0x5bc16 (called out of line from _Insert); copy 0x43eb5, copy_backward 0x43e72
//  - deque() is a no-argument ctor over a _Deque_val<_Ty, _A> base (as vector): the out-of-line copy 0x7ba1e
//    (UIManager ctor) takes no argument and copies its own allocator temporary
//  - insert(P, X) 0x95eaf (exe EECPUnitManager): push_front/push_back at the ends, else a copy of X, push_front(front())
